{"term":"cópula","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_generic","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The most formally clinical Portuguese term for copulation, from Latin 'copula'; used in medical, zoological, and legal texts.","english_term":"copulation","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"In Brazilian Portuguese grammar, 'cópula' also denotes a linking verb (e.g., 'ser', 'estar'), which keeps this usage firmly academic; lay speakers virtually never use it for sex."}
