{"term":"foder","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_generic","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The primary Brazilian Portuguese crude verb for sexual intercourse; the functional and emotional equivalent of English 'fuck' in both sexual and expletive uses.","english_term":"fuck","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Also a versatile general-purpose expletive and intensifier mirroring the full semantic range of 'fuck'; among the most commonly heard vulgarities in Brazil across all demographics."}
{"term":"trepar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_generic","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Very common crude slang verb for sexual intercourse; literally 'to climb/mount', evoking the physical act.","english_term":"to screw / to bang","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Slightly less intense than 'foder'; the transparent 'climbing' metaphor contributes expressiveness; used across all age groups in informal speech without strong taboo avoidance."}
{"term":"transar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_generic","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The most common colloquial verb for having sex in Brazilian Portuguese; relatively neutral in register compared to 'foder' or 'trepar'.","english_term":"to have sex / to sleep with","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Can also mean 'to deal', 'to hang out', or 'to be involved in something' depending on context; when sexual intent is clear it is widely used without strong vulgarity; the safe midpoint between clinical and crude."}
{"term":"meter","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_aggressive","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for sexual penetration in the active role; literally 'to insert/put in', foregrounding the physical act of insertion.","english_term":"to stick it in / to nail","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Grammatically positions the penetrating partner as the agent; 'ele meteu nela' frames the act as the man inserting himself into the woman; the directional/inserting semantics make the active role structurally obligatory."}
{"term":"comer","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_aggressive","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for having sex in the dominant/penetrating role; literally 'to eat', metaphorically framing sex as masculine consumption or conquest of the passive partner.","english_term":"to bang / to nail / to have","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Culturally loaded with dominance and conquest; the partner who 'eats' is always the active agent; direct counterpart to 'dar'; central to Brazilian honor-shame sexual dynamics where penetrating is an act of power and being penetrated is submission."}
{"term":"dar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"anal_sex_receptive","concept":"anal_sex_receptive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for taking the receptive/passive role in penetrative sex; literally 'to give', framing the passive partner as yielding their body; most strongly associated with anal receptivity.","english_term":"to give it up / to bottom","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The antonym of 'comer'; 'ela dá' implies she takes the receptive role. In discussions of male homosexuality 'dar' specifically implies anal receptivity. Central to the Brazilian honor-shame matrix where any act of being penetrated, regardless of gender, connotes submission."}
{"term":"tomar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"anal_sex_receptive","concept":"anal_sex_receptive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for receiving penetration during sex; literally 'to take/receive'; most unambiguous in the phrase 'tomar no cu' (to be anally penetrated).","english_term":"to take it / to get it","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Semantically ambiguous in isolation — active-voice 'tomar' can mean to take/conquer someone (penetrating), while 'tomar no cu' is unambiguously receptive. The receptive/passive sense dominates in sexual slang contexts."}
{"term":"bombar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_aggressive","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for vigorous sexual intercourse; literally 'to pump/bomb', emphasizing forceful rhythmic thrusting.","english_term":"to pound / to pump","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Narrower than 'foder' in that it specifically connotes high-intensity energetic intercourse; also used for other vigorous physical activities (working out, dancing at a club), so context typically disambiguates the sexual meaning."}
{"term":"bicar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"oral_sex","concept":"oral_sex_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":48,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":63,"recognition_pct_peak":63,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang verb for oral stimulation of a partner using lips and tongue; from 'bico' (beak/tip), evoking the pecking motion; also used for passionate kissing or, in some regions, intercourse.","english_term":"to go down on / to eat out","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The beak/pecking etymology gives a lighter, more playful register than direct equivalents; regional variation determines whether it refers to oral sex specifically or to intercourse more broadly; the intercourse reading is reinforced when 'bico' is understood as the penile glans."}
{"term":"safar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_generic","concept":"intercourse_success","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":50,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":45,"recognition_pct_peak":62,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang verb meaning to successfully have sex with someone; related to 'safado' (licentious, shameless), implying obtaining sexual gratification through boldness or cunning.","english_term":"to score / to get lucky","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Derived from 'safado' (lewd/impudent person); the verb implies succeeding at a licentious act rather than simply describing sex; more dated than 'transar'; recognition appears to be declining among younger speakers."}
